# Figure policy: the vector figures consumed by LaTeX (paper/figures/*.pdf) and
# the graphical abstract are committed so that a fresh clone with only a TeX
# distribution can build the manuscript. `make figures` and
# `make graphical-abstract` regenerate them byte-identically on the locked
# environment. The raster figure previews are convenience outputs and are not
# committed. `paper/graphical_abstract.png` is the one raster exception: it is
# tracked alongside `paper/graphical_abstract.pdf` (neither is matched by the
# `paper/figures/*.png` ignore rule below) because the submission package
# requires a raster graphical abstract.
!paper/graphical_abstract.pdf
paper/figures/*.png
artifacts/*.xlsx
artifacts/bundles/

